WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.441
Some people use dogs for hunting. Many blind people use dogs as guides.

2
00:00:05.442 --> 00:00:10.690
The police use dogs to help them search. But most people keep dogs as pets.

3
00:00:10.691 --> 00:00:14.280
There is an old saying that "a dog is a man's best friend."

4
00:00:14.281 --> 00:00:22.775
Of all animals, dogs perhaps have the best relationship with people, and this friendship between people and dogs has deep roots.

5
00:00:22.776 --> 00:00:27.864
In fact, dogs and humans have been companions for about 14,000 years.

6
00:00:27.865 --> 00:00:31.948
Most scientists believe that today's dogs evolved from wolves.

7
00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:41.927
"Evolved" means that they started as wolves and then, generation by generation, they slowly changed into dogs.

8
00:00:41.928 --> 00:00:48.255
According to scientists, dogs today are very different from wolves because of thousands of years of change.

9
00:00:48.256 --> 00:00:54.761
While most dogs are friendly to humans, wolves are fierce predators, one of the most dangerous animals around.

10
00:00:54.762 --> 00:00:59.772
So how might wolves have evolved into friendly dogs?

11
00:00:59.773 --> 00:01:04.592
About 14,000 years ago, humans did not live in cities or towns.

12
00:01:04.593 --> 00:01:07.554
People didn't even have farms to grow food.

13
00:01:07.555 --> 00:01:15.826
Instead humans hunted animals for food and moved from place to place, looking for the best hunting grounds.

14
00:01:15.827 --> 00:01:23.306
The animals that humans hunted were the same animals that wolves hunted, so wherever the people went, the wolves would go as well.

15
00:01:23.307 --> 00:01:29.810
Humans and wolves were certainly not friends, but they weren't enemies either.

16
00:01:29.811 --> 00:01:34.058
In the evenings humans would light fires to cook their meals.

17
00:01:34.059 --> 00:01:40.272
Some wolves would smell the delicious odor of cooking meat and try to sneak close the fire to get food.

18
00:01:40.273 --> 00:01:44.565
If a wolf did not seem threatening, people would give it some of their leftovers.

19
00:01:44.566 --> 00:01:49.870
Humans especially liked the wolf cubs because they seemed cute and friendly.

20
00:01:49.871 --> 00:01:54.799
Other wolves would come to garbage piles and eat the food thrown away by the people.

21
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.570
As long as the wolf wasn't threatening, humans were glad to let it clean up the garbage.

22
00:01:59.571 --> 00:02:07.458
So, after many generations, humans and wolves began to develop a good relationship.

23
00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:10.635
Some wolves began to live near human camps.

24
00:02:10.636 --> 00:02:16.442
Humans liked these camp wolves because they had a much better sense of smell and hearing than the humans.

25
00:02:16.443 --> 00:02:23.083
When the wolves smelled or heard an unfriendly animal or unfriendly group of humans coming, they would bark.

26
00:02:23.084 --> 00:02:25.350
This would warn the people in the camp.

27
00:02:25.351 --> 00:02:31.187
Today protecting people from unfriendly animals and strangers is the job of a guard dog.

28
00:02:31.188 --> 00:02:33.759
Camp wolves were the first guard dogs.

29
00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:38.578
But not all wolves became camp wolves; some were too wild and fierce.

30
00:02:38.579 --> 00:02:44.174
Only the friendly wolves were accepted by the people in the camp.

31
00:02:44.175 --> 00:02:47.745
People eventually began to take care of the friendly wolves.

32
00:02:47.746 --> 00:02:50.849
They would give them food and a dry place to sleep.

33
00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:55.687
Scientists think that the shape of these animals changed over time.

34
00:02:55.688 --> 00:03:01.300
Since the wolves no longer had to hunt for food, their heads and teeth probably became much smaller.

35
00:03:01.301 --> 00:03:06.993
Dogs that were kept in northern areas probably began growing long, thick fur to keep them warm.

36
00:03:06.994 --> 00:03:11.150
Meanwhile, dogs living in the south lost hair to help them stay cool.

37
00:03:11.151 --> 00:03:14.362
The friendship between humans and dogs strengthened quickly.

38
00:03:14.363 --> 00:03:20.322
Dogs began to help people on their farms. They also helped people hunt.

39
00:03:20.323 --> 00:03:24.066
Soon humans began to raise dogs simply for companionship.

40
00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:27.395
Today there are hundreds of different kinds of dogs.

41
00:03:27.396 --> 00:03:32.821
Some dogs, like the Doberman pinscher, are large and used as guard dogs.

42
00:03:32.822 --> 00:03:40.078
Other dogs, like the poodle and cocker spaniel, are small, usually harmless, and kept simply as pets.

43
00:03:40.079 --> 00:03:45.800
All dogs are similar in that they are tamable, which means they will act friendly to humans.

44
00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:49.782
They are trainable, which means they will do what people tell them to do.

45
00:03:49.783 --> 00:03:58.206
Also unlike wolves, dogs often wag their tails in a friendly way.

46
00:03:58.207 --> 00:04:05.931
But what is most amazing is that, unlike any other animal, dogs may exist only because they are useful and friendly to humans.

47
00:04:05.932 --> 00:04:10.198
Maybe if there were no humans in the world, there would be no dogs either.

48
00:04:10.199 --> 00:04:18.050
Most scientists believe that thousands of years of living with people led dogs to evolve from fierce, wild wolves into tamable, trainable,

49
00:04:18.051 --> 00:04:25.120
and tail-wagging friends.

